   "stem": {
      "text": "Water flows into a tank at the rate \\( R(t) = 3 \\sin{\\left(\\frac{t^{2}}{6} \\right)} + 14 \\) gallons per hour, where t is measured in hours for \\( 0 \\le t \\le 7 \\). The tank holds 40 gallons of water at time \\( t = 0 \\). During the same time, water flows out through a drain at the rate \\( D(t) = t + 7 \\) gallons per hour. Using a calculator, find the total number of gallons that arrive during the time interval \\( 2 \\le t \\le 6 \\). Show the setup, and give the value correct to three decimal places.",
